{
  "_readme": "Saved permission decisions CAPTURED from the installed runtimes, rather than written by hand (RL-001): five cases on September 14, 2026; Grok Build, Qwen Code and Oh My Pi on September 23, 2026; Codewhale, Kiro and Cline on September 24, 2026; and Kimi Code on October 30, 2026. Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Kilo and Pi approved the same operations on their own on the first day, so they have no case. Each case states the two halves that the Worker stores for one answer: request, the provider section of supplemental_content, and response, the agent's own bytes. prompt is the control prompt that the Worker records in the row's metadata (control_prompt): agent.ReadControlPrompt of the request with no transcript row, as protojson, with a permission's input_json compact. label is what the transcript row reads, measured in a cold browser. TestSavedDecisionCorpusPrompts (backend/internal/worker/agent/providers) reads each request through its provider and requires the stated prompt, and frontend/src/components/chat/savedDecisionCorpus.test.ts replays each case through the provider's controlResponseDisplay with that prompt and requires the label. A runtime that changes its wire shape therefore fails a case instead of quietly degrading a reloaded row to the generic \"Responded\". The worker metadata is otherwise absent: it carries a per-request claim token, which is a credential, and the displayed words never derive from it.",
